Write a general SQLite SELECT query implementing this contract on any valid dataset. Return exactly {"query":"your SQL"}. The query will run against several different hidden datasets with this schema, including empty matches, ties and missing children. Do not hard-code the representative rows. Cents amounts are nonnegative integers; customer/order foreign IDs always reference existing rows, and every interval has start_at < end_at. Use only SELECT/CTEs, joins and deterministic SQLite functions; no recursion, metadata, extensions, PRAGMAs or writes. Column aliases are irrelevant; column order, row order, NULLs and integer values are checked exactly. No parameters.
Allowed functions: abs, avg, coalesce, count, dense_rank, first_value, ifnull, instr, lag, last_value, lead, length, lower, ltrim, max, min, nth_value, nullif, rank, replace, round, row_number, rtrim, substr, substring, sum, total, trim, typeof, upper. CASE and CAST expressions are allowed.
For every active customer, return customer_id and net_cents: the sum of paid order amounts minus all refunds belonging to those paid orders. Include active customers with no paid orders as integer zero. Refunds can have several rows per order; do not multiply order amounts. Sort customer_id ascending.
Schema:
CREATE TABLE customers (customer_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, region TEXT NOT NULL, active INTEGER NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE orders (order_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, customer_id INTEGER NOT NULL, day INTEGER NOT NULL, status TEXT NOT NULL, amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE refunds (refund_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, order_id INTEGER NOT NULL, amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL);
Representative dataset (column order follows the schema):
