Candidates are the distinct people appearing in skills. Return one column person for candidates having every skill in requirements, including all candidates when requirements is empty. Extra skills are allowed. Sort person ascending.
Schema:
CREATE TABLE requirements (skill TEXT PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE skills (person TEXT NOT NULL, skill TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(person, skill));
Representative dataset (column order follows the schema):
{"requirements":[["sql"],["review"]],"skills":[["Ada","sql"],["Ada","review"],["Ada","design"],["Ada","ops"],["Bo","sql"],["Bo","design"],["Bo","ops"],["Cy","sql"],["Cy","design"],["Cy","ops"],["Dee","sql"],["Dee","review"],["Dee","design"],["Dee","ops"],["Eli","sql"],["Eli","review"],["Eli","design"],["Eli","ops"]]}

